    {
      "id": "1521",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1521,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "を以て can be though of as a formal version of the basic particle で when used to mean 'at this point in time', e.g. これ（で・を以て）閉会します ('With this, we will end the meeting.'). Note that をもって would not typically be used with the meaning of で indicating 'place of an action', e.g. 大手企業で働く 'to work at a major corporation'.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 784,
          "slug": "をもって",
          "title": "をもって",
          "meaning": "As of, With, Effective from",
          "level": "JLPT1",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
        "second_relatable": {
          "id": 36,
          "slug": "で-by",
          "title": "で",
          "meaning": "With, By (using)",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
